  "description": "Fuselage: Fire-engine red all over, belly included. Tail: Red fin; its lower half a navy panel edged in gold along the top and the forward side, carrying 'FIRE DEPARTMENT' in an arc of gold capitals, 'CITY OF NEW YORK' in white and a white skyline with the twin towers along the root. The gold edge runs on down the aft fuselage, and behind it a US flag (navy canton with white stars at the top, red and white stripes) wraps the fuselage under the fin; red tail-cone tip. Engines: Red with white 'jetblue.com', polished lips. Winglets: Red wingtip fences. Titles: Large white 'jetBlue' forward; 'Blue Bravest' small below the cockpit. Artwork: FDNY panel and US flag.",
